-- title:
--   The chart kernel is not the σ-twisted Gauss centre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$ and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K_2$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image under the coefficient map $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield generated by the ratios `intFormRatiosC` of $\Gamma_0(Mp)$, let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating that maximal ideal, and let $K_2$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j_2 \in K_2$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of $j(q)$, and let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K_2$ characterised as the Gauss ring: $f \in W_0$ iff $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$ for some power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal. Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K_2$ with $\sigma(j_2)$ the expansion of $j(q^p)$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho$ be a ring homomorphism from the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ (the elements of $K_2$ integral over $A[j_2]$) to the subfield of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by $j(q)$ and $j(q^M)$, with $\rho(\varpi) = 0$ and $\rho$ sending $j_2$ to the generator $j(q)$. The conclusion is that it is not the case that for every $b$ in the chart algebra, $b \in \ker \rho$ holds if and only if $b$, viewed in $K_2$, lies in the nonunits of the pullback $\sigma^{-1}(W_0)$ of the Gauss ring along $\sigma$.
--
--   In the analysis of the reduction modulo $p$ of $X_0(Mp)$ into two sheets interchanged by the Atkin–Lehner/Frobenius twist, this rules out one of the two possible identifications: the prime of the chart algebra cut out by a homomorphism carrying $j_2$ to the $j$-generator of the level-$M$ function field in characteristic $p$ cannot be the centre of the Frobenius-twisted Gauss valuation ring, since the residue class of $j$ there would be a $p$-th power while $j(q)$ has $q$-order $-1$. It is used to force the untwisted alternative in [`ModularCurve.XZeroPM.mem_ker_iff_coe_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_of_map_jChartFin_eq_jGeomGen_gamma0_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XZeroPM.mem_ker_iff_coe_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_of_map_jChartFin_eq_jGeomGen_gamma0_mul).
